WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.850
<b>Winter Colors, Illumination Display Special Report
 Kyoto</b>

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.390
<i>The most amazing illumination displays
 add color to Kyoto's winters.</i>

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.190
I was just thinking, "It's Halloween, huh?"

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.860
And now the city is already 
full of illumination displays.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.700
It's so crowded around times 
like Christmas. It makes things tough.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.010
Oh, right. Itsuka, when's your birthday?

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.960
What's this all of a sudden?

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.570
I was just thinking about how 
Christmas is Christ's birthday,

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.500
and I realized that I didn't know 
when your birthday is, Itsuka.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.700
It's passed.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.550
Huh?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:33.430
It passed before you came 
back home, Nagomu-san.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:38.380
Why'd you have to phrase that 
so misleadingly? You gave me a nasty shock!

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.190
That means it's still coming up, right?

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.020
In that case, about celebrating it...

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.020
What do you think about going 
out somewhere together that day?

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.020
<i>That's exactly the reaction 
I thought she'd have.</i>

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.920
Saki-kun!

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.030
It didn't work out again!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>Mizuo</b>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>Yuzu</b>

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.240
You can say it with a smile now, I see.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:11.840
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.720
<b>Long-Awaited Warmth of Spring</b>

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.080
If it's about her birthday...

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.930
Couldn't you ask the mistress and the others?

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:43.440
If someone Itsuka hasn't told 
knew when her birthday was,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.180
I'm sure she'd be put off.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.640
Yes, put off completely.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:49.580
Okay. Assignment complete!

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.580
Nagomu-san, you're really 
skilled at juicing yuzu.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.150
They've made me help with 
it since I was little.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.770
So it's juicing yuzu more than 
seeing illumination displays

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:02.140
that makes me feel like December is here.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:07.280
My family likes Ryokushou's yuzu yokan, 
too, so I send it to them every year.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.160
Thank you. We look forward 
to your continued patronage.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.920
Since we're talking about it, 
when's your birthday, Nagomu-san?

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.670
Me? The fifteenth of this month.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.280
Then it's coming up soon! I'm sorry!

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.400
Don't worry about it. At my age, 
there's no need to count the years anyway.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.430
But, let's see...

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:28.770
Saki-kun, if you'd dress as a girl 
and go drinking with me, then...

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.770
I will not.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.270
Nagomu-san! Someone from the florist is here.

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:36.270
Whoa, that's huge! What's with
 the giant fir tree?

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.750
I've come to deliver it as a present.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.270
A present?!

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.960
<i>Could it be that a rich older man 
with long legs sent it just for me?</i>

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.790
On the message card, it says, "To Itsuka."

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:50.040
I'm back!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.290
Welcome home!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.080
A fir tree.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:59.050
Here.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.170
To Itsuka

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.550
Mama...

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.910
<i>Itsuka, are you well?</i>

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.010
<i>This fir tree is a slightly 
early Christmas present.</i>

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.240
<i>I've sent it with permission 
from the mistress of Ryokushou.</i>

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.740
<i>I'll be coming back to 
Japan for Christmas Eve.</i>

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:18.820
Itsuka, are you well?
 This fir tree is a slightly early Christmas present. 
I've sent it with permission from the mistress of Ryokushou.
 I'll be coming back to Japan for Christmas Eve. 
If it's all right with you, Itsuka, could I see you?
 From Mama

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:18.820
<i>If it's all right with you, 
Itsuka, could I see you?</i>

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.390
<i>From Mama.</i>

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.700
I'm so sorry!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.380
I didn't mean to read over your shoulder, 
but these eyes of mine just...

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.620
What do I do?

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.230
What do you mean? Go ahead and see her.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.460
If you're worried about work, there's no need.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.340
I'm a little scared of making a promise.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.340
<i>Itsuka,</i>

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.300
I promise we'll be together 
for your birthday, all right?

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:53.810
<i>I'm sorry, Itsuka! Some work came 
in that I just have to get finished!</i>

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:56.060
<i>You'll be okay on your own, right?</i>

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.320
<b>To my beloved mama</b>

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.820
I'm home, Itsuka!

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.800
I'm sorry. We'll start your 
celebration now, with Papa, okay?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.580
Mama wasn't good at promises.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.920
<i>Itsuka's mother...</i>

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.880
<i>It's been five years since she left.</i>

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.250
<i>When she couldn't locate Itsuka, 
she came looking for her.</i>

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.910
<i>They were finally reunited not long ago.</i>

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.840
<i>I thought she'd take Itsuka with her, but...</i>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.700
<i>She must be scared of the distance 
that time has put between them.</i>

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.600
Don't worry.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.290
Even if it doesn't work out, 
you'll be able to forgive her, right?

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:40.610
Given who you are now, Itsuka.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:43.900
If you want insurance, I'm here.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:49.150
Please send Mama a text saying,
 "I'll be waiting."

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:50.410
Roger that.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.120
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.120
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.600
Yesterday wasn't, but today's really cold.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:00.170
Well, I guess I should complete 
my assignment again today.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.630
<b>Mizuo</b>

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.630
<b>Yuzu</b>

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.890
The juicer broke?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:16.300
It cracked with a snap.

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.980
You didn't leave it out 
with water on it, did you?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.150
I d-did it right! I left it to dry 
in a well-ventilated area!

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:28.650
Then it must have reached the end of 
its life. It's been thirty years, after all.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.200
Thirty years...

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.910
We can manage for today's batch,
 but for the future...

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:33.800
Fuki!

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:34.890
Yes?

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:36.830
Where's Dad's order ledger?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.280
I'll look for it.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:39.130
Hey...

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.420
How did we juice them before we had this?

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.670
Why do the both of you look so dumbfounded?

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.390
You don't remember?

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.170
Remember what?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.800
What a heartless child.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:51.340
What are you talking about?!

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:55.260
Never mind. This is fresh yuzu yokan.
 Go give it to your grandpa.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.270
<i>This year, the winter solstice 
is on the 22nd again.</i>

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:03.270
<i>Nagomu's birthday is one week before that.</i>

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:07.030
<i>That's right. I heard something from Grandpa.</i>

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:11.640
<i>He said I was supposed to 
have been born on the 22nd.</i>

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:15.950
The winter solstice is also called 
"long-awaited warmth of spring."

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.890
It's when the sun's power is
 at its very weakest,

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:22.920
but starts to grow stronger 
again day by day.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:26.210
They say that strong scents keep 
bad energies at bay, you see.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:30.220
So, during this time, we use yuzu's 
strong fragrance to cleanse ourselves.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:34.300
That's the significance behind yuzu baths.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:37.390
Wow. I thought it was to 
keep from catching a cold.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.010
I mean, it makes you all nice and warm.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:42.230
A cold is one type of bad energy.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.360
Peaches and chestnuts take three years,
 but persimmons take eight.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.770
And yuzu take nine years to bear fruit.

00:07:47.770 --> 00:07:48.980
What? Why?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.740
Just as the saying states, yuzu takes 
a lot of time and effort to bear fruit.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:58.350
So, when I heard that your 
due date was the 22nd,

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:02.660
I just <i>knew</i> I had to make 
some kind of yuzu sweet.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.910
And that's why you bought this.

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:05.920
That's right.

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:10.590
Then I should've waited a 
little longer to be born.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.820
Idiot.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.330
I couldn't stand waiting anymore.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:15.930
That's why you came early, right?

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.220
And you came home from
 the hospital one week later,

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.930
exactly on the winter solstice.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:25.180
<i>There isn't a child who is more 
devoted to his grandpa than you.</i>

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:27.440
<i>Thank you, Nagomu.</i>

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.660
That's right, Grandpa.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.190
I remember now.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.370
I'm sorry I broke it, Grandpa.

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:38.330
Nagomu! What are you doing? 
Hurry up and come help!

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:45.830
Then that means that this yuzu yokan 
is made every year for you, right?

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:51.050
What a lovely story. To think of someone 
coming up with a sweet for your birthday...

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.340
That's true if it were the 
story and nothing else.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:57.710
Because of that sweet, I've had 
to help juice yuzu every year.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.640
I hated it!

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:02.650
It's cold, and my fingers hurt, 
and it stings, and it's boring...

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.200
And of course they made me 
do it on my birthday, too.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:07.820
Other than the cake, it was just a regular day.

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.610
To say nothing of Christmas!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.860
This is Japan!

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.540
That's what he said to me!

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.600
I thought that decorated trees and 
whole roast chickens might be mythical.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:19.870
My grandpa said the same thing.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.740
But that fir tree is amazing, right?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.750
Yeah! And that's why I'm super excited!

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.520
Leave the decorating to me!
 I'll do a perfect job!

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.130
Dad...

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.630
I'll look for somewhere 
that can repair the juicer.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.140
<b>Confectionery and Breadmaking
Kitchen Equipment Catalog</b>

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:40.140
We've used it for so long, 
I feel attached to it.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.760
Do as you like.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.640
Okay.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.400
Kanoko-san!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:51.710
You must've worked hard today. 
Are you on your way home?

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.730
Are you on your break, Kanoko-san?

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.110
Oh, stop teasing.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:59.460
I've been passing out fliers about our 
new products to our regular customers.

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:05.720
That's right. I went around to Ryokushou, 
so I saw it. That big fir tree.

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:06.830
That's just like your mother.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:10.210
I've heard that they decorate 
with real European firs overseas.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.720
In France, especially, the norm 
is to spend time with family.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.420
I'm sure that your reply must 
have made your mother very happy.

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:20.360
Which means...

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.440
On that day... Do you 
think Nagomu will be free?

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:29.150
Oh, no, since this is his hometown, 
he might spend it with friends!

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.640
I haven't heard about anything in particular.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.400
I mean, it's fine either way!

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.030
I thought I might ask him about it tomorrow,

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.090
but since he hasn't spent a 
birthday at home in a while,

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:41.070
I didn't think I should intrude.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:42.070
What?

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.670
Tomorrow's the fifteenth. 
It's Nagomu's birthday, right?

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:50.200
<i>Uh-oh. She didn't know?</i>

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:53.520
Nagomu-san's birthday is tomorrow...

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.340
Should we pretend you never heard about it?

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.840
Usually he tries to get other people's 
attention about stuff like that.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.980
<i>It's not working. She's not the 
type that can separate things out.</i>

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:08.560
But it makes me happy that you 
care for Nagomu like that.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.350
Th-That's not what this is!

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:11.810
It's just...

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:19.070
I was stubborn about something, 
and it's bothering me.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:23.660
I think those feelings of yours are 
enough to make him really happy.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:26.480
Plus, he always used to say...

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.160
"If I'm not alone on my 
birthday, that's enough."

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:33.820
And that just having someone to spend 
his birthday with made him happy.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.170
I'm back.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.180
Hey, welcome home!

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.820
Go look at the tree in the garden!

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.140
Hiiro-chan decorated it for us!

00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:48.250
It really is nice. Suddenly, 
it feels like Christmas.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.390
Huh? What's wrong?

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:52.040
Nothing!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:52.970
What?

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.170
Saki-kun...

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.150
Maybe we shouldn't have 
decorated it without asking first?

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.150
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.150
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:15.900
Good morning.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.920
You scared me! What is it?

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:21.800
Here.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.800
<b>Happy Birthday</b>

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.800
Huh? What?!

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.660
Did I tell you when my birthday is?

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.300
Oh, what could it be? A card?

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:31.810
<b>Exclusively for Nagomu-san
3/26
Going Somewhere Together
 Ticket</b>

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.310
March twenty-sixth? Is that date...

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:38.190
Let me just say that if you lose it,
 it becomes invalid, okay?

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:43.310
Okay. It's a promise.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.410
If you're lying, I'll make 
you swallow a thousand yokan.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:52.780
That'd be rough.

